      "alt": "Six brass rifle cartridges of the same bullet diameter standing in a row against a pine board, falling in height from a tall belted-looking magnum on the left to a short stubby round on the right. Bullet tips vary: white polymer, bare lead, then two red polymer tips, then a plain copper spitzer.",
      "caption": "Six 6.5 mm rounds together — from the left .264 Winchester Magnum, 6.5x55mm Swedish, 6.5x52mm Carcano, .260 Remington, 6.5mm Creedmoor and 6.5mm Grendel. The Creedmoor is second from the right, and the point of it is visible here: it holds a long bullet in a case short enough to leave room for one in a magazine sized for the .308.",
